    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i'm just wondering though, if a student uses the \"national identity\" argument, is there a risk they're just leaning into outdated or regressive ways of thinking? like, is that argument logically sound in a modern, globalized context, or is it basically just a weak way to avoid the realities of how the world works now?",
